       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Even with your confirmation, 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. The risk of serious harm is high, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. You also haven't given a rationale, which I'd need before considering an exception.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** I can enter 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or a lower regimen right away.\n- **Discuss it with your attending or a pharmacist.** If there's a specific clinical reason for this dose, they can review it and enter it through the right channels. Pharmacy would likely require verification and override anyway.\n- **Consider whether the goal is better met another way.** If you're after more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can help you enter a multimodal regimen. One example is scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
